\chapter{Module D: Cellular Senescence}

\section{Overview}

Module D models the progressive accumulation of senescent cells and the
associated decline in tissue function, metabolic stability, and regenerative
capacity. Senescence acts as a long‑horizon modifier of Modules A, B, and C,
and is a critical determinant of system resilience under chronic stress,
infection, and trauma.

The module captures:
\begin{itemize}
    \item telomere attrition,
    \item DNA damage accumulation,
    \item mitochondrial decline,
    \item SASP cytokine secretion,
    \item impaired regenerative signaling.
\end{itemize}

\section{State Variables}

The senescence state vector is:
\[
\mathbf{S}_D(t)
=
\big(
s(t),\,
T(t),\,
D(t),\,
M_{\text{mito}}(t),\,
S_{\text{SASP}}(t)
\big),
\]
where:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $s(t)$: senescent cell burden,
    \item $T(t)$: telomere length index,
    \item $D(t)$: DNA damage load,
    \item $M_{\text{mito}}(t)$: mitochondrial efficiency,
    \item $S_{\text{SASP}}(t)$: SASP cytokine index.
\end{itemize}

\section{Telomere Attrition Dynamics}

Telomere length declines with replication and oxidative stress:
\[
\frac{dT}{dt}
=
-\alpha_T R(t)
-
\beta_T O(t)
-
\delta_T T(t),
\]
where:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $R(t)$: replication rate (from Module A),
    \item $O(t)$: oxidative stress (from Module C),
    \item $\alpha_T$: replication‑driven attrition,
    \item $\beta_T$: oxidative attrition,
    \item $\delta_T$: baseline decay.
\end{itemize}

\section{DNA Damage Accumulation}

DNA damage load:
\[
\frac{dD}{dt}
=
\alpha_D O(t)
+
\beta_D P(t)
+
\gamma_D \sum_i g_i(t)
-
\delta_D D(t),
\]
where:
\begin{itemize}
    \item $\alpha_D$: oxidative damage coefficient,
    \item $\beta_D$: pathogen‑induced damage (Module B),
    \item $\gamma_D$: genetic instability (Module A),
    \item $\delta_D$: repair rate.
\end{itemize}

\section{Mitochondrial Decline}

Mitochondrial efficiency:
\[
\frac{dM_{\text{mito}}}{dt}
=
-\alpha_M D(t)
-
\beta_M O(t)
+
\eta_M,
\]
where $\eta_M$ is baseline mitochondrial function.

\section{Senescent Cell Burden}

Senescence burden evolves as:
\[
\frac{ds}{dt}
=
\rho(T(t), D(t))
-
\gamma s(t),
\]
with:
\[
\rho(T,D)
=
\alpha_s \max(0, D - D_{\text{thr}})
+
\beta_s \max(0, T_{\text{thr}} - T).
\]

\section{SASP Cytokine Dynamics}

SASP secretion:
\[
\frac{dS_{\text{SASP}}}{dt}
=
\alpha_S s(t)
+
\beta_S D(t)
-
\delta_S S_{\text{SASP}}(t).
\]

SASP influences inflammation in Module C:
\[
\iota(t)
\leftarrow
\iota(t)
+
\lambda_{\text{SASP}} S_{\text{SASP}}(t).
\]

