\section{Summary}

Module D provides a comprehensive model of cellular senescence, integrating
telomere attrition, DNA damage, mitochondrial decline, SASP secretion, and
senescent cell burden. Its long‑horizon influence on Modules A, B, and C makes
it essential for predicting chronic deterioration, resilience, and
countermeasure effectiveness.